    "created_at": "2022-06-22T16:09:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-22T16:10:00Z",
    "body": "Does this hold for the inverse: when the `<dialog>` is in a shadow root, but the `<form>` is in the light DOM? e.g.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<my-dialog>\r\n  #shadow-root\r\n    <dialog><slot></slot></dialog>\r\n\r\n  <form method=\"dialog\">\r\n    <button type=\"submit\">Close?</button>\r\n  </form>\r\n</my-dialog>\r\n```\r\n\r\nif it's intentional, that's a shame, since i expect it will be very common for people to wrap <dialog> in their own component\r\n\r\nedit: adapting the original example\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n  <head>\r\n    <script>\r\n      window.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\r\n        const div = document.querySelector(\"div\");\r\n        const shadow = div.attachShadow({ mode: \"open\" });\r\n        shadow.innerHTML = \"<dialog open><slot></slot></dialog>\";\r\n      });\r\n    </script>\r\n  </head>\r\n  <body>\r\n    <div>\r\n      <form method=\"dialog\">\r\n        <button>Close</button>\r\n      </form>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </body>\r\n</html>\r\n```",
